   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Days, hours and syntactic investment",
   "texto": [
    "The days of the week in Dutch are: maandag (Monday), dinsdag (Tuesday), woensdag (Wednesday), donderdag (Thursday), vrijdag (Friday), zaterdag (Saturday), zondag (Sunday). To ask the time: «Hoe laat is het?» (What time is it?) and to answer: «Het is acht uur» (It's 8: 00 o'clock). Gold rule of investment!: if you start the sentence with a time supplement like «Vandaag», the verb is placed in second position and the subject passes to the third: «Vandaag is het maandag» (and never * Vandaag het is...)."
   ]
